      "updated_at": "2026-03-27T23:15:44Z",
      "body": "Thanks for the quick response @evshary!\n\nWe actually already follow this pattern in our SDK \u2014 our Zenoh subscriber callbacks only enqueue messages to an asyncio queue (`loop.call_soon_threadsafe(queue.put_nowait, ...)`), and all `session.get()` calls run on a separate `ThreadPoolExecutor` via `run_in_executor()`. The Zenoh rx threads are never blocked by application logic.\n\nDespite this architecture, we still see intermittent zero-reply returns from `session.get()` in peer-to-peer multicast mode. The behavior is consistent with routing-table staleness \u2014 when a queryable is active and responding, `session.get()` sometimes determines \"no responders\" instantly (well before the timeout), as if the queryable isn't in the local routing table at that moment.\n\nWe've worked around it with `QueryTarget.ALL` (to bypass routing-table lookups and broadcast to all peers) plus application-level retry, which substantially improves reliability. But the underlying issue seems to be that the multicast routing table for queryables has a staleness window that pub/sub routing doesn't have.\n\nCould this be a routing-table synchronization issue in multicast scouting mode, separate from the callback-blocking scenario?",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
